From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:18:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] feat(users): let admins change a user's role

The template had roles but no way to change one short of an SQL update,
which then applied only at the account's next refresh.

PATCH /api/users/:id (admins only) changes the role and raises the
account's securityVersion in the same transaction: its access tokens end
at once and its next refresh carries the new role, its sessions go on.
The last admin cannot stop being one (409); a demotion locks every
admin's row in one order first, so two admins demoting each other at
once cannot both succeed, nor deadlock.

Each name on the list of users opens the account's page
(/admin/users/:id, lazy, with a budget of its own: 1.1 kB), where an
admin changes the role.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
